---
/**
 * Your wall.
 *
 * The route that loses orders, which is why it is a route rather than a line in the checkout.
 * A customer whose walls are in modern emulsion cannot use any of these four products without
 * stripping first; telling them after they have paid produces a return, a bad review and a wall
 * that is now worse than it was.
 *
 * The matrix is the page. Everything else on it exists to make the matrix readable.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Painted from '../components/Painted.astro';
import { PAINTS, SUBSTRATES } from '../data/paints';
import { colourBySlug } from '../data/colours';
import images from '../assets/images.json';

const hex = colourBySlug.get('flax')!.hex;
const limewashed = images.find((image) => image.slug === 'limewashed')!;
const counts = SUBSTRATES.map((substrate) => ({
  substrate,
  yes: PAINTS.filter((paint) => substrate.on[paint.id].verdict === 'yes').length,
  no: PAINTS.filter((paint) => substrate.on[paint.id].verdict === 'no').length,
}));
const refusals = counts.reduce((total, entry) => total + entry.no, 0);
---
<Base
  title="Your wall — Marlpit"
  description="What each Marlpit paint may go on, and what it may not. A substrate matrix that refuses rather than upsells."
  hex={hex}
  chapter="Substrates"
>
  <Painted hex={hex}>
    <div class="page">
      <div class="head2">
        <div>
          <p class="label">Before you choose a colour</p>
          <h1 class="display display--sm">What is already on the wall decides most of this.</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="prose small">
          Thirty-two combinations of four paints and eight substrates. {refusals} of them are a
          straight no, and the most common wall in Britain — sound modern emulsion over gypsum —
          is four of those noes. We would rather tell you here than at the checkout.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Painted>

  <Painted hex="#ede8da">
    <div class="page">
      <table class="tbl mtx">
        <caption class="mtx__cap">
          Each cell is what that paint may do on that substrate, and why. Read the reason: a
          &ldquo;prep&rdquo; that needs the render taken off is not the same job as a
          &ldquo;prep&rdquo; that needs a thinned first coat.
        </caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Substrate</th>
            {PAINTS.map((paint) => <th scope="col">{paint.name}</th>)}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {SUBSTRATES.map((substrate) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" class="mtx__sub">
                {substrate.name}
                <span class="mtx__note">{substrate.note}</span>
              </th>
              {PAINTS.map((paint) => {
                const cell = substrate.on[paint.id];
                return (
                  <td class="mtx__cell" data-verdict={cell.verdict} data-paint={paint.name}>
                    <span class:list={['verdict', `verdict--${cell.verdict}`]}>
                      {cell.verdict === 'yes' ? 'Yes' : cell.verdict === 'prep' ? 'With prep' : 'No'}
                    </span>
                    <span class="mtx__why">{cell.why}</span>
                  </td>
                );
              })}
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </Painted>

  <Painted hex="#2f2820">
    <div class="page emul">
      <figure class="emul__fig">
        <img src={limewashed.small} width="900" height="600" loading="lazy"
             alt="A limewashed rubble-stone house, its wall bright white and slightly uneven." />
        <figcaption>{limewashed.usedAs}. Photograph {limewashed.photographer}, {limewashed.licence}.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="label">The answer nobody wants</p>
        <h2 class="head">If it is in emulsion, it has to come off.</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            Lime will not bond to a plastic film, and it would not help if it did — the film is the
            thing stopping the wall drying outward, so painting over it with something breathable
            changes nothing except the colour.
          </p>
          <p>
            On plaster that usually means steaming and scraping, then letting the wall dry for as
            long as it takes, which can be months on a wall that has been sealed for a decade. It
            is a real job and it is the reason a lot of people decide not to do this. We would
            rather you decided that now.
          </p>
          <p>
            If the emulsion is sound and you are not able to take it off, use a good vapour-open
            emulsion from somebody else and do not buy from us. That is a genuine recommendation
            and not a rhetorical one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Painted>

  <Painted hex={colourBySlug.get('oxblood')!.hex} band>
    <div class="page ask2">
      <p class="head ask2__h">Not sure what you have?</p>
      <p class="prose small">
        Send us photographs of the wall, a corner where the layers show, and the age of the
        building. We will tell you what we think is on it and whether any of this is worth doing.
        <a class="u" href="/samples">That, and the sample pots →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </Painted>
</Base>

<style>
  .display--sm { font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 1.2rem + 2.4vw, 3.25rem); max-width: 19ch; }
  .label + .display--sm { margin-top: var(--s4); }
  .head2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(var(--s5), 4vw, var(--s8)); align-items: end; }

  .mtx__cap { text-align: left; max-width: 66ch; padding-bottom: var(--s6);
    font-size: var(--t-small); color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 78%, transparent); }
  .mtx thead th { vertical-align: bottom; }
  .mtx__sub { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; padding-right: var(--s5);
    width: 22%; vertical-align: top; }
  .mtx__note { display: block; font-family: var(--body); font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--t-label); line-height: 1.45; margin-top: 4px;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 62%, transparent); }
  .mtx__cell { width: 19.5%; }
  .mtx__cell[data-verdict='no'] { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 5%, transparent); }
  .mtx__why { display: block; margin-top: var(--s2); font-size: var(--t-label); line-height: 1.5;
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 74%, transparent); }

  .emul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(var(--s6), 4vw, var(--s9)); align-items: start; }
  .emul__fig { margin: 0; }
  .emul__fig img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; object-fit: cover; }
  .emul__fig figcaption { margin-top: var(--s3); font-size: var(--t-label);
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 62%, transparent); }
  .emul .head { margin-top: var(--s3); }
  .emul .prose { margin-top: var(--s5); }

  .ask2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(var(--s5), 4vw, var(--s8)); align-items: baseline; }
  .ask2__h { max-width: 14ch; }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .head2, .emul, .ask2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s5); }
    .emul__fig img { aspect-ratio: 16 / 10; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    /*
     * Eight rows by four columns of reasoned cells does not narrow. It becomes eight records,
     * each listing its four verdicts — which is how somebody uses this page anyway: they know
     * their wall and they want to know which of the four they may buy.
     */
    .mtx, .mtx tbody, .mtx tr, .mtx td, .mtx th, .mtx caption { display: block; width: 100%; }
    .mtx thead { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); }
    .mtx tr { padding-block: var(--s5); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line-strong); }
    .mtx__sub { width: auto; padding: 0 0 var(--s3); font-size: var(--t-sub); }
    .mtx__cell { width: auto; padding: var(--s3) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .mtx__cell[data-paint] .verdict::after { content: ' · ' attr(data-paint); font-weight: 500;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em; text-transform: none;
      color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 62%, transparent); }
  }
</style>
